the last time I saw you, right?

00:00:08.953 --> 00:00:11.490
- Thank you, yeah, I've
been doing a lot better.

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:14.020
- [Interviewer] So you're no
longer living on the street?

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:14.930
- No, sir, I'm not.

00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:16.440
I'm not on Skid Row anymore.

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:17.690
- [Interviewer] You're in an apartment?

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:18.880
- I am, I am.
- That's great.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:23.565
- Yeah, yeah, I'm in the
area, but I'm not in downtown.

00:00:23.565 --> 00:00:24.717
- [Interviewer] Yeah, but
having a roof over your head

00:00:24.717 --> 00:00:25.550
is a really nice thing, right?

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:26.960
- That's a fact, that's a fact, yeah.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.140
My health has been doing better.

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:29.760
I got real sick for awhile,

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:32.340
but just symptomatics in my
stomach, and all that stuff,

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:37.170
but I've been cleaned up,
pretty much off of everything.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:40.970
And weed, except for, and cigarettes.

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:43.646
But yeah, I haven't really been,

00:00:43.646 --> 00:00:45.040
I haven't been around it.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:46.700
- [Interviewer] So you're
last talk was very heavy.

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:48.550
- Very much so, yeah.

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:50.041
- [Interviewer] Very, very,

00:00:50.041 --> 00:00:51.510
it was traumatic just
watching you go through it.

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:53.110
- Yeah, it's hard to think about,

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:54.943
and I can't watch the...

00:00:54.943 --> 00:00:57.043
- [Interviewer] And how
did that talk affect you?

00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:58.833
- Ooh.

00:00:58.833 --> 00:01:03.050
I still have, I guess,

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:05.170
flashbacks will be the clearest memories,

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:06.826
I guess, that kind of deal.

00:01:06.826 --> 00:01:08.600
- [Interviewer] Of what
you were talking about?

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:11.016
- Right, right, and just yeah.

00:01:11.016 --> 00:01:12.450
- [Interviewer] That's hard to talk about.

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:14.360
- Yeah, and for whatever reasons,

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:15.820
like really loud noises,

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:18.210
even cars or just something booming,

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:20.780
just instills a terror in me.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.360
So I'm not sure why,

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:24.670
but I still wake up everyday,

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:27.630
and like I said, grab
the world by the cojones

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:28.850
and say, "Let's go!"

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:30.090
Why not?
(Glow laughing)

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:30.960
- [Interviewer] So a while back

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:33.430
I helped you out a little
bit to get a motor home,

00:01:33.430 --> 00:01:35.110
but you've yet to do that, right?

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:36.190
- Not yet, yeah.
- Yes.

00:01:36.190 --> 00:01:37.400
- It's still in the works.
- It's still in the works.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:38.880
Okay, great.
- Yeah.

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:41.464
- [Interviewer] So where
does your life go from here?

00:01:41.464 --> 00:01:43.275
Where do you think...

00:01:43.275 --> 00:01:47.460
- Well, it's wide open actually.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:49.380
Like I said, the RV is the goal,

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:52.970
to have a home that you can travel in

00:01:52.970 --> 00:01:55.070
but one that it's yours.

00:01:55.070 --> 00:01:57.500
And then I might go back to school

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:00.230
just for some psychological
or even art classes.

00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:02.180
Just to, you know, maybe, I don't know.

00:02:03.059 --> 00:02:06.330
But I'm thinking also of
going up to the woodsy area

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:09.223
or maybe going up to Washington maybe.

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:11.073
I'm not sure yet.

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:14.440
- [Interviewer] The
world, the whole country

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:16.100
is your oyster.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:17.515
- Kinda!
- You can go where you want.

00:02:17.515 --> 00:02:18.747
- Yeah, kinda.

00:02:18.747 --> 00:02:21.023
But things have been going really well.

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:24.360
In fact, the gal that I had met

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:28.474
through a mutual friend of
ours was the lady that offered,

00:02:28.474 --> 00:02:32.520
with her roommate, offered
to let me move in with them.

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:33.870
So I was grateful for that.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:36.690
She and I get along real
well, and the other roommate,

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:38.052
we all get along real well.

00:02:38.052 --> 00:02:38.910
- [Interviewer] It's nice
to have some friends, right?

00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:40.970
- Yeah, yeah, been fortunate.

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:42.043
So, yeah.

00:02:44.352 --> 00:02:46.490
- [Interviewer] And you were
on Skid Row for how long?

00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:49.581
- Almost a year, almost a year.

00:02:49.581 --> 00:02:51.938
- [Interviewer] What do
you make of Skid Row?

00:02:51.938 --> 00:02:52.771
- Oh.

00:02:52.771 --> 00:02:53.666
(Glow nervously laughing)

00:02:53.666 --> 00:02:56.193
- [Interviewer] How was your
year living here in a tent?

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:01.120
- It was interesting to say the least.

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:03.203
Terrifying to say the least.

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:06.330
An experience like none other,

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:07.860
I don't believe anyone could ever get

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:10.760
unless they were out
here to experience it.

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:11.900
And to this day,

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:14.620
just about everything I
still see and experience

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:17.010
is something I've only ever seen on TV.

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:18.810
So my jaw will still hit the ground.

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:23.180
I tried it out here,

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:27.561
but I'm convinced that when
you don't have a good health,

00:03:27.561 --> 00:03:31.190
to be strong out here, it
really makes a difference.

00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:32.310
- [Interviewer] I think the
stress of being down here

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:34.030
maybe wears you down.

00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:34.970
- Definitely.

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:36.040
- [Interviewer] The filth of Skid Row

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:37.300
